==English==
{{wikipedia|River Thames}}
{{wikipedia|Thames, New Zealand}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|Temese}}, from {{inh|en|ang|Temes}}, {{m|ang|Temese}} (cognate with {{cog|cy|Tafwys}}), from {{der|en|la|Tamesis}}, possibly from {{der|en|cel-pro|*Tamesas}}, from {{der|en|cel-pro|*tamēssa||dark}}<ref>{{R:ine:EIEC|147}}</ref>. Compare {{cog|cy|tywyll||darkness}} and {{cog|ga|teimheal}}, from {{der|en|cel-pro|*temeslos||darkness}}. Possible cognates include river names such as [[Teme]], [[Tavy]],[[Teviot]], [[Teifi]].

Alternatively from unknown non-Indo-European root<ref>{{cite-book|1955|Jackson, Kenneth H.|The Pictish Language|chapter=The Problem of the Picts|editors=Wainright, F. T.|location=Edinburgh|publisher=Nelson|pages=129–166}}</ref><ref>{{cite-journal|1998|Coates, Richard|A new explanation of the name of London|Transactions of the Philological Society|volume=96|issue=2|url=http://www.blackwell-synergy.com/doi/pdf/10.1111/1467-968X.00027|doi=10.1111/1467-968X.00027|pages=203–229}}</ref> or from {{der|en|cel-pro|*ta-||to melt}} indicating "muddiness"<ref>{{cite-journal|1996|Kitson, Peter R.|British and European River Names|Transactions of the Philological Society|volume=94|issue=2|doi=10.1111/j.1467-968X.1996.tb01178.x|pages=73–118}}</ref>.

